# Committed HTML-era curation pipeline (plan §7/§10.4). These are deliberately TRACKED —
# the reconstruction must be reproducible and served on any checkout / on Railway:
#   history-curation.json            queue          (deterministic prepare; the page's input)
#   history-auto-decisions.json      auto baseline  (cheap-LLM + matcher agreement, pre-fill)
#   history-curation-proposals.json  frontier hints (gpt-5.5 suggestions for uncertain cases)
#   history-decisions.json           human choices  (saved from the curation page; apply input)
#   history-curation-llm-cache.json  resume cache   (prior LLM/frontier asks; lets capped runs continue)
#   history-reintroductions.json     reintro ledger (hand-authored; #117 revived-name docs → seam:reintroduced)
#   history-html-era.json            applied freeze (synced to atlas_history by build:history)
#   history-pre-era.json             pre-git origins (mip/genesis/severed — docs/plans/
#                                    pre-git-history.md; scripts/prehist/*, synced by build:history)
# Regenerated deliberately (reviewed reruns), then committed. The audit/trace write to .cache/.
